WEBVTT

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:09.650
We acquire the legendary dragon's card in the world of Duel Monsters.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:13.870
But we don't know anything about our enemies.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:18.100
Pegasus sends me an invitation to come to America.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:22.370
If I meet him, I may learn who our enemies are.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:26.770
Meanwhile, Kaiba is also going to meet Pegasus.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:48.070
Before I knew it, I abandoned happiness to survive

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:55.210
Lying to myself, I danced clinging on to illusions

00:00:55.990 --> 00:01:01.870
At the edge of my vision when I close my eyes

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:07.860
I was searching for your smile

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:15.230
With our memories fading

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:22.310
We hold on to our dreams and run  Yeah

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:29.210
These feelings that I shut away in my heart

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:36.440
I'll now grasp them again

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:03.330
Toon World's Nightmare

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:16.580
Look!  We're almost in San Francisco!

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:20.750
I'm so excited!  This is my first trip to America!

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.840
We're not here to sightsee.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:26.440
You seem nervous, partner.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:30.560
After seeing the video, I'm worried about Pegasus.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.280
I think someone is after him.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.800
I'm worried too.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.210
Yeah.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:56.450
I never thought I'd come to Duelist Kingdom again.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.130
Big brother.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.950
All I have are bad memories.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.400
No one's here.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.630
Then no one will bother us.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.150
Let's go, Mokuba.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.260
A cable car!

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:20.900
Like the movies!

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:29.050
I see the Golden Gate Bridge!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.200
Now I feel like I'm really in America!

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:34.400
Right, Yugi?

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.960
Huh?  What?

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:38.120
What's wrong?  Thinking about something?

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:42.260
Yeah.  What was Pegasus trying to tell me?

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:49.100
Monsters appeared around the world, my God Cards were stolen...

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.420
...and Doma's Three Musketeers showed up.

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:58.670
And both our world and the Duel Monsters' world are in danger.

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:01.750
Pegasus must know something.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.680
But what?

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:31.520
How rude!  You invite me, but you don't show up?

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.580
Stop playing and show yourself!

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:41.450
Welcome, Kaiba boy!  It's been a while!

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:54.760
Nice to meet you, Kaiba boy.  And...

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:56.700
Mokuba boy.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.700
You finally showed up, Pegasus.

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:02.380
I need to check something with you.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.050
Why?

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:09.200
Industrial Illusions is responsible for the events worldwide, right?

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.130
What?

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:11.590
Don't play dumb!

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:16.810
Duel Monsters are turning real and causing chaos!

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:22.490
Kaiba Corporation's Solid Vision System isn't malfunctioning!

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:28.730
So the perpetrator can only be you - the creator of Duel Monsters!

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.170
Are you sure?

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:32.460
What?

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:37.410
Kaiba boy, it's all your fault.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:38.720
What?

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.630
Answer me!  What do you mean?

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:48.280
If you want the answer, you must defeat me in a duel.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:49.540
How dare you!

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:52.960
I remember when I dueled you before.

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:58.280
You were desperate to save Mokuba boy's soul.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:04.600
Mokuba boy's soul is sealed in this card.

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:15.680
Kaiba boy, if you defeat me, I will release Mokuba boy's soul from this card.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:21.600
But you couldn't defeat me.  And then...

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:28.000
Kaiba boy, you know what happens when you lose the game, right?

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:34.400
The loser loses everything he holds dear, including himself.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:38.970
You will share the same fate as Mokuba boy!

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:40.620
Mind Card!

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:47.210
Be quiet!

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:50.950
Why are you upset, Kaiba boy?

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:53.150
I'm just telling the truth.

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:59.630
You want to fluster me by reminding how you humiliated me, but it won't work.

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:03.090
Bring it on, Pegasus!  Let's end this!

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:05.600
Fine, Kaiba boy.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:08.900
Let's have a great duel!

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:30.190
Since you came all the way to Duelist Kingdom, I set up the old Duel Ring.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.120
Because you want revenge.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:38.290
Whatever system you use, I don't trust you.

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:40.920
I'm using this!

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:46.200
If we duel fair and square, I won't lose to you twice!

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:49.740
That's right!  My big brother won't lose to you!

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:55.040
Fine.  We'll soon know if you're right or not.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:57.480
Mokuba, stay back.

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:00.160
But big brother...

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:03.420
Pegasus may have traps set.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:07.880
Big brother...

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:11.460
I dreamed for this day to come.

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:23.390
He sealed away his duelist's fighting spirit.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:26.350
But he's now going to set it free.

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:30.010
Big brother!  Beat Pegasus!

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:35.820
Are you going to use your trick to see my hand again?

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:38.820
No!  Don't worry.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:43.630
I can beat you easily without scanning your mind.

00:09:43.630 --> 00:09:47.300
Keep talking!  I'll win no matter what you do!

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:52.170
Big brother...

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.100
Duel!

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:04.500
I'll go first.  I draw.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:08.560
I summon a monster in defense position.

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:11.550
That card...

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:14.360
And I set a card.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.290
I end my turn.

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:19.230
How cheap.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:21.660
What?  Why?

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:26.330
Trying to fluster me by using the same strategy as before?

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:28.770
Oh?  Is that what I'm doing?

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:31.940
Sorry.  I forgot.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:36.530
I told you.  I've changed.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.810
Your psychological warfare won't work!

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:40.440
My turn!

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:45.180
I summon Spear Dragon in attack position!

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.660
Attack Toon Alligator!

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:57.000
Due to Spear Dragon's effect...

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:01.200
...if its attack points are greater than your defending monster's defense points...

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:05.340
...you take the difference as damage!

00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:10.270
After it attacks, it switches to defense position.

00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:13.980
I set two cards.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:16.420
I end my turn.

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:18.350
Nice, big brother!

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:37.610
P.U.!

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:43.220
Ouch...

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:52.010
Where...

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:52.890
...are we?

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:55.280
Help me!

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:11.710
It's my turn!

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:16.380
Oh!  This card will be fun!

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:21.820
I activate the spell card, Toon Table of Contents!

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:23.750
Toon Table of Contents?

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:30.270
I can add a card with "Toon" in its name from my deck to my hand.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:32.360
What?  You don't mean...

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:34.850
Yes, I do.

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:36.960
Well done, Kaiba boy.

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:39.250
You guessed correctly.

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:41.840
My invincible card is...

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:44.000
Toon World!

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:51.450
Kaiba boy, I re-invite you to the world of perfect creatures.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:56.640
I pay 1000 life points to activate Toon World!

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:04.830
I summon Toon Masked Sorcerer!

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:13.200
Only Toon monsters can block the attacks of other Toon monsters.

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:16.970
Toon World punished my brother before.

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:19.580
How will my brother fight it?

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:24.010
Regular attacks can't destroy Toon monsters!

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:28.950
You think the same strategy will work against me again?

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:32.160
I activate my trap!  Cloning!

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:35.590
Kaiba boy also has a Toon monster?

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:37.960
Attack if you want.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:41.130
The Toon monsters will just destroy each other.

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:42.800
Goddamn!

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:48.820
My brain holds all data from my past duels.

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:54.280
I've already calculated how to defeat you.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:56.240
I end my turn.

00:13:56.570 --> 00:13:57.980
My turn!

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:01.180
I won't fight how you want me to!

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:05.620
I tribute Toon Masked Sorcerer and Spear Dragon.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:08.290
What?  What are you going to do?

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:12.900
I summon Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.640
My brother's Blue-Eyes!

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:24.570
Blue-Eyes and I will win together!

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:26.280
That was pointless!

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:30.740
Blue-Eyes can't attack my Toon!

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:32.970
I'm not afraid of Toons!

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:35.420
I told you my dueling was perfect!

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:38.550
I activate my set trap!

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:43.040
Toon Mask.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:46.300
By tributing a Toon monster on my field...

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:51.750
...I Special Summon a Toon copy of your monster!

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:52.900
What?

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:56.160
Here's Blue-Eyes Toon Dragon!

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:02.690
Blue-Eyes Toon Dragon!

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:06.110
How dare you show me that detestable thing again!

00:15:06.110 --> 00:15:09.130
That's not a nice thing to say.

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:13.050
I told you that I can deal with your Toons!

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:16.990
I activate my spell card!  Shrink!

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:23.960
Blue-Eyes Toon Dragon's attack points are halved to 1500!

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:27.070
But Toons are invincible.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:29.940
Using Shrink to lower its attack points is pointless!

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:35.110
From my hand, I activate the Continuous Spell, Charm of Lamentation!

00:15:38.110 --> 00:15:43.000
Blue-Eyes White Dragon attacks Toon Dragon!

00:15:43.660 --> 00:15:49.130
That won't work!  Making the same silly mistake again?

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:52.360
Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:15:57.340 --> 00:16:02.250
Forget that regular attacks don't work against Toon monsters?

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:05.050
I know that.

00:16:05.050 --> 00:16:06.840
I have a different goal!

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:08.310
Why?

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:10.710
The Continuous Spell, Charm of Lamentation.

00:16:10.710 --> 00:16:16.420
When my monster fails to destroy your monster during my Battle Phase...

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:20.220
...I can add a card in my deck to my hand.

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:25.480
My deck has a key card to destroy Toon World.

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:27.830
I must draw it as soon as I can.

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:29.760
It's my turn!

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:38.200
I pay 500 life points so that Blue-Eyes Toon Dragon can attack Kaiba boy directly!

00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:42.750
You don't have a Toon monster on your field!

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:45.540
You can't block this attack!

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:49.950
I flip over my spell, Negate Attack!

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:52.750
Oh no!

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:58.760
Your monster's attack is negated, and the Battle Phase ends!

00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:02.070
No matter if your monster is a Toon or not!

00:17:02.070 --> 00:17:07.400
Then I activate the spell card, Toon Rollback!

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:14.680
It lets me have two Battle Phases!

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:18.840
No way!  A monster can attack only once per turn.

00:17:18.840 --> 00:17:22.720
Even if you have a second Battle Phase, it can't attack again.

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:24.730
That's correct.

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:26.570
But...

00:17:26.570 --> 00:17:30.360
I haven't summoned a monster this turn yet!

00:17:30.580 --> 00:17:31.530
What?

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:36.460
If I summon a new monster, it can attack with no problems.

00:17:36.460 --> 00:17:44.350
I tribute Blue-Eyes Toon Dragon to summon Toon Dark Magician Girl!

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:57.980
Attack him directly!

00:17:57.980 --> 00:17:59.360
Yes, Master!

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:08.530
No way!  He instantly lost 2000 life points!

00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:12.990
How's that!  My Toons have evolved!

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:16.740
My turn!  I draw!

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:20.700
Blue-Eyes attacks Toon Dark Magician Girl!

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:28.580
Blue-Eyes can't destroy a Toon.  Why's he attacking?

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:46.810
Charm of Lamentation lets me draw a card.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.360
What's so funny?

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:54.890
A perfect creature?  You make me laugh.

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:58.520
You disgrace your reputation as the creator of Duel Monsters.

00:18:58.520 --> 00:18:59.250
Why?

00:18:59.720 --> 00:19:02.250
Toon monsters are invincible.

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:05.250
But only when Toon World protects them.

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:09.190
So I'll destroy Toon World!

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:10.860
Toon World?

00:19:10.860 --> 00:19:14.290
I activate the spell card, A Wingbeat of Giant Dragon!

00:19:17.650 --> 00:19:18.780
What?

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:23.470
I return a Level 5 or higher Dragon to my hand...

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:27.690
...to destroys all spell and trap cards on the field!

00:19:28.130 --> 00:19:32.950
Your precious Toon World is gone!

00:19:44.060 --> 00:19:45.860
My Toon World...

00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:47.420
All right!

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:49.800
There's no card I can't defeat!

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:52.130
Wow, big brother!

00:19:53.430 --> 00:19:57.210
I summon Versago the Destroyer in defense position!

00:19:57.990 --> 00:19:59.170
I end my turn!

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:05.810
Who are you?

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:14.520
My anti-Toon strategy is perfect, but you should've been ready for it.

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:19.460
Your strategy is a copy of our previous duel.

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:23.780
The Pegasus I know isn't that dumb.

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:26.160
You're not Pegasus!

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:29.120
Who are you?  Tell me!

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:32.100
Impressive, Seto Kaiba.  You figured me out.

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:35.710
You're right.  I'm not Pegasus.

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:37.640
What's going on?

00:20:45.310 --> 00:20:48.490
I'm Amelda, one of Doma's Three Musketeers!

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:51.110
Doma's Three Musketeers?

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:53.250
I can't forgive you.

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:54.930
What are you talking about?

00:20:55.180 --> 00:20:59.370
I'll get my revenge, Seto Kaiba!

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:05.970
I activate The Seal of Orichalcos!

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:12.680
What?

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:17.160
What's this?

00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:26.220
What's this?

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:28.160
The Seal of Orichalcos.

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:35.330
Once you're trapped in this seal, you can't escape unless you win the duel.

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:40.770
And the Seal will seal away the loser's soul.

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:42.310
What?

00:21:42.540 --> 00:21:44.010
Seto Kaiba.

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:51.320
Under Doma leader Dartz's orders, I will take your soul!

00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:08.720
The streets flow by, colored in red

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:17.060
If you notice your pain, it changes to joy

00:22:18.790 --> 00:22:28.220
People learn of friendship every time they wipe their tears

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:37.740
With the warm strength you gave me, I'll change them into kindness

00:22:38.310 --> 00:22:46.770
My overflowing emotions don't stop

00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:52.280
I'll live feeling them

00:22:52.890 --> 00:22:57.460
For me to be me

00:22:57.460 --> 00:23:05.920
Overflowing friendship heals me

00:23:06.600 --> 00:23:11.560
Our chance meeting was real

00:23:12.080 --> 00:23:21.220
We'll both understand that someday

00:23:27.570 --> 00:23:31.680
We came to America because Pegasus invited us.

00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:36.850
But our vehicle drives out of the city and on to remote roads.

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:40.320
Industrial Illusions is in the middle of nowhere?

00:23:41.060 --> 00:23:44.730
Meanwhile, fake Pegasus reveals his true identity.

00:23:44.730 --> 00:23:48.570
Amelda seems to hate Kaiba.

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:50.960
What happened in the past?

00:23:50.960 --> 00:23:53.520
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Awaken!  Critias

00:23:53.520 --> 00:23:55.040
Duel, standby!
